## Metallic and Chrome Finishes to Try This September

Getting a chrome nail finish at home starts with a fully cured, tack-free gel base, since chrome powder only grabs onto a flawless surface. The powder is buffed on with a silicone applicator or brush in small circular motions, then sealed under a no-wipe top coat. Skipping the smoothing step is the most common reason a home chrome attempt turns out streaky instead of mirror-bright.

Chrome powder finish is a mineral pigment applied dry over cured gel polish, distinct from the polish color underneath it, and it is what produces that liquid-metal, mirror-like reflection. It reads differently depending on the base shade: chrome over a nude reads soft and molten, chrome over black reads hardware-store metallic, chrome over a jewel tone reads closer to poured glass. That last combination has real range this September, and pairs directly with <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/september/september-birthstone-nails'>how sapphire and jewel-tone pairings work across september nail looks</a> if you want the birthstone angle without going full stone-set nail art.

