## Which September Nail Art Texture Lasts the Longest

Cat-eye gel and standard chrome finishes hold up the longest without chipping, typically 2 to 3 weeks with correct prep, because both are sealed entirely under gel and top coat with no exposed raised elements to catch on fabric or hair. Hand-painted and 3D dimensional work wears shorter, usually closer to 10 to 14 days, since edges and raised accents are the first thing to lift.

Matte sits in the middle of the pack for chip resistance but needs the most upkeep to look intentional rather than worn, since a matte top coat starts picking up shine at the tips within a week even when the polish underneath hasn't chipped at all. Glass and jelly finishes are durable in the sense that they resist chipping well, but they show growth at the cuticle line faster than opaque finishes do, simply because the sheerness that makes the effect work also makes the gap more visible.

The real durability variable across every texture here is prep, not the finish itself. A dehydrated nail bed and a properly cured base coat add more wear time than switching finishes ever will.

